+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is The Market Common part of Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every home in it is inside the City of Myrtle Beach, so the city's zoning and tax rate apply. Nearly every home has a Myrtle Beach mailing address in ZIP code 29577."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I rent out a Market Common home by the night?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The town center's zoning district is one of the city's zones for rentals under 90 days; the neighborhoods around it are not. Each HOA's rules also decide, and we read them for the home you pick."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I buy one of the apartments over the shops?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The apartments above the town center's shops are rented by the year. The area's 37 condos are in High Market, south of Valor Park."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far is The Market Common from the beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"About 5 minutes by car with no traffic, to the city's beach access at 29th Avenue South. On foot it is about 45 minutes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What was The Market Common before?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Myrtle Beach Air Force Base, which closed in 1993. The town center opened on part of it in 2008."}}]}</script>
