.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 11.5 12 4.5l8 7M6.5 10v4.5M17.5 10v4.5M2 17c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 20.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>Homes in a high-risk flood zone</strong><span class="t">2 percent</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span><span><strong>Beach by car, no traffic</strong><span class="t">About 5 min</span></span></li></ul><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero mc-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-town-center-homes-over-shops-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1099px) 100vw, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="A four-story building with shops on the ground floor and apartments with balconies above, on a street in The Market Common" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: DiscoA340. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: DiscoA340</a></span></div><figcaption>Homes over the shops in the town center. These apartments are rented by the year, not sold.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">A town center with shops, a lake and a movie theater, built on the old Myrtle Beach Air Force Base, with about 3,000 homes in the neighborhoods around it.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common is a town center with shops, restaurants, a movie theater and a lake, built on the former Myrtle Beach Air Force Base. About 3,000 homes stand in it and in the neighborhoods around it, all inside the City of Myrtle Beach. In the past year a house there resold for about $525,000 at the middle, and a townhome for about $375,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses list an HOA fee of $150 a month or less, while townhomes on the town center's streets list more than $300. Only 2 percent of homes are in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. No home is inside the line where the airport's yearly average noise reaches 65 decibels.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Want the homes for sale here, sorted by neighborhood?</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us send the list</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#what-it-is" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What it is</a></li><li><a href="#homes" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Kinds of home</a></li><li><a href="#prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Prices</a></li><li><a href="#yearly-cost" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Yearly cost</a></li><li><a href="#flood" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Flood zones</a></li><li><a href="#airport-noise" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Airport noise</a></li><li><a href="#walk" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Walking and driving</a></li><li><a href="#compare" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Compared</a></li><li><a href="#the-market-common-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The Market Common FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-it-is"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What it is">What is The Market Common in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common is the town center of the former Myrtle Beach Air Force Base, a 3,936-acre base that closed in 1993. The old base now holds The Market Common and its neighborhoods, Myrtle Beach International Airport, Whispering Pines Golf Course, a technology and aerospace park, and a dozen parks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The base began as the town's airport. The Army made it a training base in World War II and closed it in 1948. The Air Force reopened it in 1956 for F-100 fighter jets and later flew A-10 "Warthog" attack planes there. From the middle of the 1970s, airline flights shared its runway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Air Force closed the base in 1993, as defense spending fell after the Cold War, and the area lost nearly 5,100 jobs. In 2019 the EPA gave the base's cleanup and rebuilding its national reuse award.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town center opened in 2008 on 121 acres between US 17 Business and the US 17 Bypass. The apartments above its shops and restaurants are rented by the year. The base's old back gate, at US 17 and Farrow Parkway, is now the Bellamy Interchange.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Three Air Force jets still stand in Warbird Park on Farrow Parkway, on permanent loan to the city: an F-100 Super Sabre, an A-7D Corsair and an A-10 Warthog.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="homes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Kinds of home">Where are the homes in The Market Common, and what kinds are there?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3,000 homes stand in The Market Common area: about 2,480 houses, 465 townhomes and 37 condos. About 570 are in the town center district, about 500 of them on its own streets. The rest are in the neighborhoods around it.</p><figure class="mc-fig"><div class="mc-frame"><svg class="mc-map mc-area-m" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="250 300 1360 800" role="img" aria-labelledby="mc-area-t-m"><title id="mc-area-t-m">Aerial map of The Market Common in Myrtle Beach. The town center, with its lake, Valor Park and rows of townhomes, sits just west of the airport's runway. The larger neighborhoods spread to the west and north-west: Cresswind, The Reserve, Emmens Preserve, Balmoral, Withers Preserve, Park Place, West Lake and Belle Harbor, out to the US 17 Bypass. The beach is to the east, past US 17 Business.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-area-aerial.webp" x="0" y="0" width="2000" height="1299" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M1164.7 896L1161.9 880.2L1183 875.7L1186.2 880.9L1191