9.4 974.9L1159.9 896.6L1126.1 902.1L1124.8 894L1109.6 896.8L1107.7 889.9L1070.9 897.9L1065 869.9L1054.4 872.1L1043.2 826.6L1092.5 815.6L1091.7 754.2L1083.9 700.3L1067.1 669L1055.8 657.1L1043 648.2L1020.1 640.8L995.6 640.2L986.1 642.9L969.9 583.9L1064.3 545L1076.8 573.2L1089.9 590.4L1138.6 581.7L1144 608.6L1135.2 610.4L1138.9 626.1L1158.2 622L1194.3 787.3L1225.9 777.7Z" fill="none" stroke="#ffe7c2" stroke-width="6" stroke-dasharray="22 11"/><circle cx="1112.3" cy="736.4" r="11" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="5"/><text class="lb" x="765" y="405" text-anchor="middle">Cresswind</text><text class="lb" x="560" y="645" text-anchor="middle">Emmens</text><text class="lb" x="560" y="683" text-anchor="middle">Preserve</text><text class="lb" x="790" y="712" text-anchor="middle">Balmoral</text><text class="lb" x="690" y="830" text-anchor="middle">Withers</text><text class="lb" x="690" y="868" text-anchor="middle">Preserve</text><text class="lb" x="870" y="930" text-anchor="middle">Park Place</text><text class="lb" x="690" y="972" text-anchor="middle">West Lake</text><text class="lb" x="330" y="905" text-anchor="middle">Belle Harbor</text><text class="lb" x="900" y="525" text-anchor="middle">The Reserve</text><text class="lb" x="268" y="700" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-63 268 700)">US 17 Bypass</text><text class="lb it" x="1905" y="1190" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-42 1905 1190)">Atlantic Ocean</text><text class="lb hl big" x="1165" y="640" text-anchor="middle">Town center</text><text class="lb hl" x="1138.3" y="750.4" text-anchor="start">Valor Park</text><text class="lb" x="1415" y="300" text-anchor="end">Airport runway</text><circle cx="1795.6" cy="952.4" r="11" fill="#fff" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="5"/><text class="lb" x="1773.6" y="930.4" text-anchor="end">Beach access</text></svg></div><figcaption>The white outlines are the neighborhoods, and the dashed line is the town center district. The dot is Valor Park, where the walk and drive times on this page start. Aerial: USDA NAIP via The National Map (USGS), public domain. Outlines: Horry County parcels and City of Myrtle Beach zoning. Map: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The largest neighborhood is Emmens Preserve, with about 730 houses and townhomes. Belle Harbor, at the west end, has about 480, and Cresswind has 400 houses. Withers Preserve, Park Place, West Lake, Balmoral and The Reserve are smaller, from about 110 to 220 homes each.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 4 in 5 homes here (81 percent) are taxed as their owner's main home: 86 percent of houses and 60 percent of townhomes. On the town center's streets about 2 in 3 are.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each kind of home costs and feels different here. The HOA fee, the monthly fee to the homeowners association that runs the neighborhood, differs most of all.</p><ul class="mc-cards" aria-label="The kinds of home in The Market Common"><li><span class="k">Most of the homes</span><b>A house in a neighborhood</b><p>About 2,480 houses, most of them in the neighborhoods west of the town center. One resold for about $525,000 at the middle. Most list an HOA fee of $150 a month or less.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Get the houses for sale in The Market Common<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></li><li><span class="k">Closest to the shops</span><b>A townhome on the town center's streets</b><p>About 240 on the town center's own streets. A townhome shares its side walls with the next one. One here resold for about $400,000, and each one for sale lists an HOA fee over $300 a month.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Get the townhomes for sale in The Market Common<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></li><li><span class="k">Rare here</span><b>A condo</b><p>Only 37 in the whole area, all in one group called High Market, south of Valor Park. One resold for about $310,000 at the middle. The apartments above the shops are rented by the year, not sold.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Ask about condos in The Market Common<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes listed under the Market Common name are on our <a href="/homes/map/?subdivision=Market%20Common" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">map of Market Common homes for sale</a>. For age-restricted communities across the area, see our <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55-plus communities guide</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">What do homes cost in The Market Common?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year a house in The Market Common resold for about $525,000 at the middle, and half sold between about $475,000 and $565,000. A townhome resold for about $375,000, and a condo for about $310,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Prices differ by neighborhood. Balmoral's houses resold for the most, about $685,000, and Emmens Preserve's for the least, about $440,000.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Neighborhood</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Kind of home</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Resold for, at the middle</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Balmoral</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $685,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The town center's own streets</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $570,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Belle Harbor</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $545,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Cresswind</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $540,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Park Place</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $525,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Withers Preserve</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $520,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The Reserve</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $520,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Emmens Preserve</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">House</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $440,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The town center's own streets</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Townhome</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $400,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Emmens Preserve</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Townhome</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $380,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">High Market</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Condo</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $310,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="mc-note">Resales recorded in Horry County deeds in the past year, in groups with 10 or more sales. The town center's streets include Sweetgrass Square.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">New homes cost more. The only builder sales in the past year were 9 townhomes on the town center's streets, at about $580,000 at the middle, about $180,000 more than a resale townhome on the same streets.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At our last count, 66 homes were for sale in the area: 43 houses asking about $530,000 at the middle and 20 townhomes asking about $420,000. You can see them on our <a href="/homes/map/?subdivision=Market%20Common&amp;type=townhouse" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">map of Market Common townhomes</a> and the <a href="/homes/map/?subdivision=Market%20Common&amp;type=house" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">map of its houses</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you own here and want to sell, our <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">home value page</a> explains how we price a home from recorded sales.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Know what a Market Common home is worth</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We pull the county's recorded sales on that street and in that neighborhood, and send you a price range.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us price a Market Common home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does a Market Common home cost to own each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Besides the mortgage and insurance, a typical house here that you live in costs up to about $3,900 a year in property tax and HOA fee. A town center townhome costs about $6,400 to $7,600 a year, mostly because its HOA fee is higher.</p><div class="mc-cost"><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year, as your main home</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">A house, about $525,000</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">A town center townhome, about $400,000</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $2,100</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $1,600</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">HOA fee</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Up to about $1,800</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $4,800 to $6,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Together</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Up to about $3,900</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $6,400 to $7,600</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The fees are what the homes for sale list: most houses $150 a month or less, and town center townhomes about $400 to $500. Before you offer, we get the HOA's budget for the home you pick, so you know what the fee covers.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, a home you live in pays about $404 a year in property tax for every $100,000 of the county's value. A second home or rental pays about $1,528, about 3.8 times as much.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">When a home sells, the county sets its value at about the price a buyer pays, so your tax starts from your price. The lower rate needs an application to the county. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax guide</a> explains both rates.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="flood"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Flood zones">Is The Market Common in a flood zone?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost none of it is. Only 62 of about 3,000 homes in The Market Common, 2 percent, sit in FEMA's high-risk flood zone. Another 30 are in the moderate zone, and the rest are in no special zone.</p><ul class="mc-rules" aria-label="Homes in the high-risk flood zone"><li><strong>Cresswind: 38 houses</strong>The largest group, near the neighborhood's ponds.</li><li><strong>Balmoral: 14 houses</strong>The second group.</li><li><strong>The town center: 10 houses</strong>On its own streets.</li><li><strong>Everywhere else: none</strong>No other neighborhood has a home in the zone.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">All 62 are in zone AE, where water rises in a big flood but big waves are not expected. A mortgage from a federally backed or regulated lender on a home in that zone requires flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Water can still reach a home outside the zones. Our page on <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">flooding a seller may not mention</a> explains how we look into a home's flood history.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Check one home before you offer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We check its flood zone, its HOA fee and its tax as a main home, and tell you what we find.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us check a home</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="airport-noise"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Airport noise">How loud is the airport next to The Market Common?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No home in The Market Common is inside the line where the airport's yearly average airplane noise reaches 65 decibels. The FAA treats homes below that level as compatible with an airport, with no limits.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The airport's own land-use drawing shows the line for today and for its forecast in 2038. We placed both on every home's lot. The closest home is about a quarter mile outside the line, on the town center's east edge.</p><figure class="mc-fig narrow"><div class="mc-frame"><svg class="mc-map mc-noise" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1600 1619" role="img" aria-labelledby="mc-noise-t"><title id="mc-noise-t">Aerial map of the town center of The Market Common and the airport next to it. A shaded band marks where the airport's yearly average airplane noise reaches 65 decibels or more. It runs along the runway and out past its south end toward the beach. The town center's homes sit to the south-west of the band, about a quarter mile from it at the closest point.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-n/submarkets-market-common/market-common-noise-aerial.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1600" height="1619" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M509.3 839.4L504.8 814.7L537.7 807.8L542.8 815.8L550.8 811L550 798.4L542.6 795.4L539.9 779.9L569.9 773.4L574.6 775.3L578.4 771.6L623.5 761.6L632 798.4L635 801.6L640.2 796.8L635.1 770.9L647