255,231,194,.5);border:2px dashed #b9863f"></i>The town center district</li></ul><figcaption>The band joins the airport's lines for today and its forecast for 2038, traced from its land-use drawing, so its edge is approximate. Aerial: USDA NAIP via The National Map (USGS), public domain. Noise lines: Myrtle Beach International Airport layout plan, sheet 14. Map: Chapter3 Realty.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The 65-decibel area runs along the runway and stretches out past both ends, where planes take off and land. Small rings of louder levels sit around a helicopter pad near US 17 Business at the runway's south end, used for oceanfront helicopter flights.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A yearly average is not a ceiling. It counts every sound from 10 p.m. to 7 a.m. as 10 decibels louder, so night flights weigh more. A single takeoff is louder than 65 decibels, and planes are heard across the area.</p><ul class="mc-rules" aria-label="How far the homes are from the airport"><li><strong>The town center</strong>The closest part. Its nearest home is about a quarter mile from the 65-decibel line, and a little over half a mile from the runway's center line.</li><li><strong>The neighborhoods to the west</strong>The nearest home in them is about 0.9 mile from the line. Homes in Belle Harbor, at the west end, are about 1.8 miles or more from it.</li></ul></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="walk"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Walking and driving">What can you walk to from The Market Common?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes on the town center's own streets are the ones within about 8 minutes on foot of the shops, measured from the middle of them to Valor Park. From the middle of the larger neighborhoods it is a 20- to 35-minute walk, and about 50 minutes from Belle Harbor.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Minutes on foot to Valor Park, from the middle of each neighborhood"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Minutes on foot to Valor Park, from the middle of each neighborhood</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Neighborhood</span><span role="columnheader">On foot</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The town center's own streets</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.136" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Sweetgrass Square</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.236" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">13 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">High Market (condos)</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.26" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The Reserve</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.365" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">20 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Park Place</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.387" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">21 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Balmoral</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.405" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">22 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Withers Preserve</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.462" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">25 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">West Lake</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.493" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">27 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Cresswind</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.531" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">29 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Emmens Preserve</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.631" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">35 min</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Belle Harbor</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.925" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">50 min</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Walking routes on OpenStreetMap streets and paths. The homes nearest the town center in each neighborhood are closer than its middle.</figcaption></figure><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero mc-side" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:720px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/del-webb-grande-dunes/market-common-lake-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/del-webb-grande-dunes/market-common-lake-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/del-webb-grande-dunes/market-common-lake-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, (max-width: 1099px) 720px, 380px" width="1200" height="800" alt="The lake and lawn at Grand Park in The Market Common in the evening" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: DiscoA340. License: CC BY-SA 4.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 4.0">Photo: DiscoA340</a></span></div><figcaption>The lake in Grand Park, beside the town center's shops. A 1.1-mile path runs around it.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town center is where people walk. These are the places in it and near it:</p><ul class="mc-rules one" aria-label="What is at the town center"><li><strong>Shops, restaurants and a movie theater</strong>Along the town center's streets, with the apartments above them.</li><li><strong>Grand Park and Valor Park</strong>Grand Park, with its lake and a 1.1-mile path around it, and Valor Park sit beside the shops. They have sports fields, picnic areas, fishing spots and Savannah's Playground, built for children of all abilities.</li><li><strong>A Saturday farmers market</strong>Held at Valor Park on Saturdays from April into December.</li><li><strong>A gym and a college campus</strong>From Valor Park, the Crabtree Gymnasium is about 11 minutes on foot, and Horry-Georgetown Technical College's Grand Strand campus about 18.</li><li><strong>Groceries</strong>The Food Lion on South Kings Highway is about a 25-minute walk, just over a mile, or about 5 minutes by car.</li></ul><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is the beach and everything else?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach is about 5 minutes by car with no traffic, at the city's beach access at 29th Avenue South, which is marked fully accessible. On foot it is about 45 minutes. Summer traffic on US 17 adds time to every drive.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">From Valor Park to</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">By car, about</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The beach access at 29th Avenue South</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">5 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Walmart Neighborhood Market, Walton Drive</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Publix, Wood Duck Drive</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">South Strand Medical Center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">7 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport terminal</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">9 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Coastal Grand Mall</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">11 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Broadway at the Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">15 min</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Grand Strand Regional Medical Center</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">20 min</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The airport terminal is across the runway, so the drive is longer than the distance looks on the map.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">See it on a Saturday</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which neighborhoods you like. We line up showings, and you walk the town center between them.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Have us set up showings</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="compare"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Compared">How does The Market Common compare with Carolina Forest and Surfside Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Market Common house costs more than one in Carolina Forest and less than one in Surfside Beach. Its townhomes cost more than either. Its share of houses in a high-risk flood zone sits between the two.</p><div class="mc-cmp"><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase"></th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">The Market Common</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Carolina Forest</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Surfside Beach</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A house, at the middle</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $525,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $440,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $745,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">A townhome, at the middle</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $375,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $230,000</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $250,000</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Houses in a high-risk flood zone</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">2.5 percent</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">0.2 percent</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 31 percent</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">By car from Valor Park, no traffic</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 25 min to its library</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13 to 14 min to its pier</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p class="mc-note">Past year. The Market Common and Carolina Forest: resales in Horry County deeds; Carolina Forest is the Census area of that name. Surfside Beach houses: every house sale in the town, its own page's figure.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carolina Forest is a much larger inland area, about 25 minutes north by car. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest guide</a> covers its neighborhoods and schools.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Surfside Beach is a beach town about 13 to 14 minutes south, where about 3 in 10 houses are in a high-risk flood zone. Our <a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach guide</a> covers its two sides of the highway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Market Common is one part of Myrtle Beach. Our <a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach guide</a> covers the city's other parts and its rules on nightly rentals.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="the-market-common-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">The Market Common FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is The Market Common part of Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Every home in it is inside the City of Myrtle Beach, so the city's zoning and tax rate apply. Nearly every home has a Myrtle Beach mailing address in ZIP code 29577.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I rent out a Market Common home by the night?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town center's zoning district is one of the city's zones for rentals under 90 days; the neighborhoods around it are not. Each HOA's rules also decide, and we read them for the home you pick.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I buy one of the apartments over the shops?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The apartments above the town center's shops are rented by the year. The area's 37 condos are in High Market, south of Valor Park.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How far is The Market Common from the beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 5 minutes by car with no traffic, to the city's beach access at 29th Avenue South. On foot it is about 45 minutes.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What was The Market Common before?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Myrtle Beach Air Force Base, which closed in 1993. The town center opened on part of it in 2008.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R729.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">air base</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R392.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">back gate</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R400.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Warbird Park</a>, <a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/myrtle-beach-air-force-base/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Encyclopedia</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/sess117_2007-2008/bills/1230.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Senate</a>, <a href="https://19january2021snapshot.epa.gov/sites/static/files/2020-01/documents/2019_award_winners_case_study.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">EPA</a>, <a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Market Common</a>, <a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/parks-playgrounds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">parks</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/find/photos_of_the_week/pow090420.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lake path</a>, <a href="https://waccamawmarkets.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">farmers market</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/services/accessibility_information/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">beach access</a>, <a href="https://aeronautics.sc.gov/sites/default/files/2025-03/14-MYR-LDU-36x48.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">airport plan</a>, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/CFR-2024-title14-vol3/pdf/CFR-2024-title14-vol3-part150-appA.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FAA rule</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/4012a" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">flood law</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county GIS</a>, <a href="https://www.cityof