+ 2007-2008 Bill 1230: Leucadia National Corporation - South Carolina Legislature Online South Carolina General Assembly 117th Session, 2007-2008 Download This Bill in Microsoft Word format Indicates Matter Stricken Indicates New Matter S. 1230 STATUS INFORMATION Senate Resolution Sponsors: Senator Rankin Document Path: l:\s-res\lar\010mark.mrh.doc Introduced in the Senate on March 26, 2008 Adopted by the Senate on March 26, 2008 Summary: Leucadia National Corporation HISTORY OF LEGISLATIVE ACTIONS Date Body Action Description with journal page number ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 3/26/2008 Senate Introduced and adopted SJ -2 View the latest legislative information at the LPITS web site VERSIONS OF THIS BILL 3/26/2008 (Text matches printed bills. Document has been reformatted to meet World Wide Web specifications.) A SENATE RESOLUTION CONGRATULATING MCCAFFERY INTERESTS, INC., LEUCADIA NATIONAL CORPORATION, MYRTLE BEACH AIR FORCE BASE REDEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY, AND THE CITY OF MYRTLE BEACH ON THE GRAND OPENING OF THE MARKET COMMON. Whereas, The Market Common, Myrtle Beach project, located at Farrow Parkway between Highway 17 Business and Highway 17 By-Pass, is the first phase and the focal point of the redevelopment program approved by the Myrtle Beach Air Force Base Redevelopment Authority and the City of Myrtle Beach; and Whereas, The Market Common is a six hundred million dollar joint venture between McCaffery Interests and the City of Myrtle Beach. This one hundred twenty-one acre multi-use development will feature the finest restaurants, retail, and entertainment establishments, complimented by beautifully landscaped parks, lakes, and a public square is surrounded by thousands of luxury town homes, condominiums, timeshares, and luxury vacation rentals; and Whereas, The Market Common is located on a three thousand seven hundred ninety acre parcel of land with thirty million dollars of new infrastructure, including twenty-nine acres of lakes, new community parks, and four miles of new roads; and Whereas, construction of The Market Common commenced in Fall 2006 with the completion date and grand opening scheduled for April 2008. Now, therefore, Be it resolved by the Senate: That the members of the South Carolina Senate, by this resolution, congratulate McCaffery Interests, Inc., Leucadia National Corporation, Myrtle Beach Air Force Base Redevelopment Authority, and the City Of Myrtle Beach on the grand opening of The Market Common. Be it further resolved that a copy of this resolution be forwarded to McCaffery Interests, Inc., Leucadia National Corporation, Myrtle Beach Air Force Base Redevelopment Authority, and the City Of Myrtle Beach. ----XX---- This web page was last updated on Wednesday, December 2, 2009 at 3:35 P.M. 
